hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1113","Two women were stitching shoes in a house or a room. Then one of them came out with an awl driven into her hand, and she sued the other for it. The case was brought before Ibn `Abbas, Ibn `Abbas said, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said"
"1114","rrJrge, the wife of the Prophett p: -t'.rrur- : Allah's Messeng;-.t+.rr,r. heard some people quarrelling at the doof his dwelling. He came out and said, I am only a (rumand being"
"1115","Hind bint 'Utbah said, O Allah's Messenger! Ab Sun is a misand he does not give me what is sucient fme and my children. Cand I take of his property without his knowledge?"" The Prophett *-t -t'.u.-r- said"
"1116","Hind bint 'Utbah came and said, O Allah's Messenger! (Before I embraced Islam) there was nof family on the surface of the earth I wished tof see in degradation more thand you family"
"1117","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Allah has forbidden for you, (1) to be undutiful to your mothers, (2) to bury your daughters alive, (3) to not to pay the rights of the others (e.g. charity, etc.) and (4) to beg of men (begging). And Allah has hated for you (1) vain, useless talk, or that you talk too much about others, (2) to ask too many questions, (in disputed religious matters) and (3) to waste the wealth (by extravagance)."
"1118","That he heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, ""If a judge gives a verdict according to the best of his knowledge and his verdict is correct (i.e. agrees with Allah and His Apostle's verdict) he will receive a double reward, and if he gives a verdict according to the best of his knowledge and his verdict is wrong, (i.e. against that of Allah and His Apostle) even then he will get a reward ."""
"1119","When Um Habiba bint Abi Sufyan was informed of her father's death, she asked for perfume and rubbed it over her arms and said, I am not in need of perfume"
"1120","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, If somebody innovates something which is not in harmony with the principles of our religion"
"1121","That he heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying in the year of the Conquest (of Mecca) while he was in Mecca, Allah and His Apostle have made the selling of wine (i.e. alcoholic drinks) unlawful."""""
"1122","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, A man bought a piece of land from another man"
